<blockquote>
<p>This is a very interesting tale surrounding the Glittering Horizons Series. Admittedly, I really lack the context surrounding the series of events with Van Turner, the Department of Photography, and everything else. Regardless, this was an extremely fun little piece. I personally enjoyed the duality between Van Turner's proposal towards the Council and Joseph being chased down by his mysterious gunman. The action between the two was definitely there and really kept me engaged throughout. The progression between the two also really flowed well for me, and the ending definitely left me wondering. Why did they do this? What's the bigger play at hand here? What's the real reason behind this all? A wonderful piece narratively, with smooth prose and detailed imagery to really nail things together. Great job author!</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Porting my feedback from the Art Exchange thread. My opinion remains unchanged. Great job!</p>

