<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Central Narrative: I haven't really thought of this, and to be honest I don't think I really need one.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You do need one yeah; you're trying to write a short story about a weird thing, not an encylcopedia entry on it; and so <em>what</em> you do with the anomaly is more important than what the anomaly does.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I want to include a long list of experimentations referencing other space-related SCPs, and possibly hint at some side effects / alternate anomalous properties this object might have along the way.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So like, what are the side effects? What are the alternate anomalous properties? What other space-related SCPs? What's tying your experiments together so it feels like a cohesive whole and not just a random series of experiments?</p>
<hr />
<p>My central concern is that as far as anomalous stuff goes, this almost feels more like an anomalous item: it has a very simple thing what it does and there's not a lot of like, things you can do to explore it. The hinting towards experiment logs could be enough to fix this but honestly I don't really have enough of a feel for what you're doing with them or how you're wanting them to be funny to tell if it'd work.</p>
</div>
