<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Post-haste our illustrious Foundation secures the area and is now able to devote its energy to a favored past-time: testing logs. Including but not limited to logs from the personnel/civilians on the ground, and logs from the Foundation's bunker where testing can be conducted on D-Class in peace.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I guess my big concern is: what are these testing logs showing? It kinda feels like they might feel&#8230;pedestrian; but I think a few showcasing the various melodies it produces could be a fun little middle section.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>We also have a neat little epilogue with the arrest of the two individuals responsible, and the return of the children to the foster care system.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Uhhh what children? Are they just a some children who are enamoured by the clock or?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>become obsessive with the clock, and may begin to prioritize listening to the chime over basic bodily needs.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>this feels to me like it's&#8230;perhaps a very dark turn for a supposedly light hearted scp to take</p>
<hr />
<p>I don't necessarily hate the idea of this; and a lot of this feels like it comes close to working; but it feels like it's missing something to just really kick it over the line and I'm not quite sure what?</p>
<p>The test logs feeling awkwardly inserted between the discovery section and the epilogue might be the core issue; but it might be that there's not a huge feeling of purpose to this: it might just need some kinda hint as to <em>why</em> the two people responsible made this and what they were intending, y'know?</p>
</div>
